 native session and official active clock. They do not fabricate a phase sample,
 immersive presentation, frame, wearer result or acoustic observation.

+## Shared-loop Start admission and recovery
+
+The selected shared breathing loop reserves the next complete cycle before
+OfficialStart. Packet-delivery liveness uses the acquisition owner's one-second
+window; the 250 ms audio-history bound remains separate. The actual admission
+still requires fresh input. A late or temporarily unready main-thread boundary
+callback may rearm its same intent for a future full cycle at most twice. It
+cannot start a completed interval or consume the pending interval's 900 seconds.
+
+Internal `defer-main` and `cancel-main` commands require the current audio
+generation, semantic revision and exact reserved frame. Cancellation preserves
+a still-valid model, selected input and audio observation. Terminal `end-main`
+keeps its existing reset semantics. Source or clock retirement cannot be undone
+by cancellation. These internal commands add no public setup or debug authority.
+
+A definitive native Start rejection cancels only the reservation captured under
+the matching carrier, native owner and complete ARMED session tuple. Duplicate
+or uncertain outcomes cannot trigger cleanup. A conclusive stale revision may
+retry cleanup once with the same generation/frame; a lost outcome is not replayed.
+Full native readback owns fenced-operation settlement, including delayed results.
+
+Focused coverage includes `test_experiment_gateway_breathing_boundary.py`,
+`test_native_start_rejection_cleanup.py`, `test_remote_durable_pending.py` and
+the real Java audio-owner/Rust runtime peer in `Test-BreathingSetupAudioHost.ps1`.
+Host checks do not establish physical Start, uninterrupted recording or data
+custody; those require the selected signed APK and an attended complete run.
+
